WEBVTT

00:06.700 --> 00:08.202
Attention, everyone,
mail call!

00:08.212 --> 00:10.662
Meg-- Teen People;
Chris-- Amazing Spiderman;

00:10.672 --> 00:11.700
Lois-- Redbook;

00:11.710 --> 00:14.107
World War II Army Guy--
a letter from your gal.

00:14.695 --> 00:17.233
Open that one up, buddy.

00:17.305 --> 00:19.075
All right,
at ease, at ease.

00:19.142 --> 00:20.410
"Dear Willy,
it's been awful lonesome

00:20.478 --> 00:22.049
since you've been away."

00:22.117 --> 00:23.385
Hey, you hear that,
fellas? She misses me!

00:23.453 --> 00:26.057
You're all wet.

00:27.463 --> 00:28.530
Hey, check this out.

00:28.598 --> 00:30.367
We got invited to a party.

00:30.435 --> 00:33.744
"Peter Griffin, you and your
family are cordially invited

00:33.811 --> 00:36.815
to a gala dinner in your honor
at Rocky Point Manor."

00:36.883 --> 00:38.854
What? What are they
honoring you for?

00:38.921 --> 00:40.860
Who cares? It says here
it's for the whole weekend.

00:40.928 --> 00:42.029
And it's free.

00:42.097 --> 00:43.432
Well, who's
the invitation from?

00:43.500 --> 00:44.803
I don't know,
it doesn't say.

00:44.871 --> 00:46.139
Wait, you're not
gonna go, are you?

00:46.206 --> 00:47.642
It's clearly
some kind of scam.

00:47.710 --> 00:49.980
Oh, well, then maybe we just go,
and you go to the kennel.

00:50.050 --> 00:51.451
Oh, not the kennel.

00:51.520 --> 00:53.523
Last time you left me
there for an hour.

00:53.590 --> 00:55.593
Or ten years, I don't know--
there's no clock there!

00:55.661 --> 00:57.265
You stink when
you come out of there.

01:07.523 --> 01:11.499
<font color="#ffff00">Captioning sponsored by</font>
<font color="#ffff00">20th CENTURY FOX TELEVISION</font>

01:11.567 --> 01:15.208
<font color="#ffff00">and</font>
<font color="#ffff00">FOX BROADCASTING COMPANY</font>

02:49.431 --> 02:51.668
Dad, are we almost there?

02:51.736 --> 02:53.439
Yeah. According to the map,
we're pretty close.

02:55.646 --> 02:58.185
Peter, look!

03:52.378 --> 03:56.590
My God, this is
absolutely beautiful.

03:56.657 --> 03:59.429
I bet Jeff Probst
has a house like this.

04:02.537 --> 04:04.575
Joe?
Peter?

04:04.643 --> 04:06.212
What the hell are
you guys doing here?

04:06.280 --> 04:09.253
Well, we got an invitation
to a dinner in my honor.

04:09.320 --> 04:12.328
I assumed it was for all
those arrests I made last month.

04:12.396 --> 04:14.834
<i>That's weird. My invitation
said it was in  my honor.</i>

04:14.901 --> 04:17.071
I assumed it was for being
able to fart the alphabet,

04:17.139 --> 04:19.409
which I almost did
till I pooped on the "S."

04:19.478 --> 04:21.313
Oh, well. Everybody
on the bus was upset

04:21.381 --> 04:22.785
long before
that anyway.

04:24.791 --> 04:25.592
What the...

04:28.665 --> 04:30.068
Derek and Jillian?

04:30.136 --> 04:31.973
Wow!
Hi, Brian!

04:32.042 --> 04:33.109
Hey, kiddo.

04:33.177 --> 04:34.578
What-- what are
you guys doing here?

04:34.646 --> 04:36.951
I got a card that says
they're throwing a dinner

04:37.019 --> 04:38.521
in my "honer."

04:38.588 --> 04:39.791
Wait a minute, what the
hell's going on here?

04:39.858 --> 04:41.530
Everybody got the
same invitation?

04:41.597 --> 04:44.870
Muriel, if you're not gonna eat
your half of the cheeseburger,

04:44.938 --> 04:47.409
I'll see if they
have a freezer, so
I can keep it nice.

04:47.477 --> 04:50.281
I'm gonna walk around;
I think my vagina's asleep.

04:57.166 --> 05:00.742
Oh. Hey.
Uh...

05:00.809 --> 05:02.679
Didn't think I'd see
anyone I knew here.

05:02.747 --> 05:05.219
This, uh, this
is Stephanie.

05:05.286 --> 05:07.390
Hi, everybody!
Oh, my gosh!

05:07.457 --> 05:10.065
I never thought I'd
meet Glenn's friends!

05:10.133 --> 05:11.902
Yeah, I figured,
why not?

05:11.970 --> 05:14.875
You know, you-- we--
you and I see each other
from time to time.

05:14.942 --> 05:18.916
Oh, my God, we, like, never
see each other! This guy!

05:18.984 --> 05:21.424
You, like, disappear for a
month, and then you call me?!

05:21.491 --> 05:22.627
So silly!

05:22.694 --> 05:25.632
You're lucky
I like you so much.

05:25.699 --> 05:28.338
Okay, why don't you go
ahead and take the bags in.

05:28.406 --> 05:31.346
Wow, it-- it looks like
the whole town got invited.

06:04.425 --> 06:06.262
Mr. Peter.

06:06.329 --> 06:07.935
Mr. Joe.

06:08.003 --> 06:09.272
Mr. Bonnie.

06:09.339 --> 06:11.242
She doesn't know
what "Mr." means.

06:11.310 --> 06:12.745
Mr. Mort.

06:12.812 --> 06:14.683
Mr. Muriel.

06:14.751 --> 06:16.319
Mayor West Mr.

06:16.387 --> 06:18.025
Oh, my God, seriously.

06:18.092 --> 06:21.132
If you will all please
follow me to third floor,

06:21.199 --> 06:23.101
I show you
to your rooms.

06:23.169 --> 06:26.375
You are all expected
for dinner at 8:00.

06:26.443 --> 06:27.881
Oh, good! I'm starved!

06:27.949 --> 06:29.685
Settle down, will ya?

06:50.167 --> 06:51.703
None of this makes any sense.

06:51.771 --> 06:54.644
Everyone got invitations
from an anonymous source

06:54.711 --> 06:56.081
for a dinner in their honor,

06:56.149 --> 06:57.585
when that's clearly
not the case.

06:57.653 --> 06:59.501
Now we're here, where
the hell's our host?

06:59.511 --> 07:02.034
Well, at least you all had
eveningwear provided for you.

07:02.128 --> 07:03.831
I thought this was
going to be a lawn party.

07:03.899 --> 07:06.139
I don't have
one pair of long pants.

07:06.207 --> 07:09.179
Boy, it's kinda awkward seeing
Jillian here with Derek.

07:09.246 --> 07:10.447
I wonder if she's
thinking about me.

07:10.515 --> 07:12.753
I don't know, are you
a pony or the color blue?

07:14.825 --> 07:16.094
Derek, look!

07:16.162 --> 07:17.866
Ha, how do you
like that?

07:17.934 --> 07:20.737
<i>Have you guys ever seen
Jim Henson's  Labyrinth ?</i>

07:20.805 --> 07:22.441
No. Have you ever seen
the Channel Five news?

07:22.509 --> 07:23.978
No.

07:24.046 --> 07:26.285
<i>Uh, Labyrinth has teenage
Jennifer Connelly.</i>

07:26.353 --> 07:29.492
Channel Five news has file
footage of pills being sorted.

07:29.560 --> 07:31.830
Some people think
Jennifer Connelly's old now,

07:31.898 --> 07:34.202
and that her hands look
like two bags of snakes.

07:34.270 --> 07:35.374
I think that's bogus.

07:35.442 --> 07:36.978
I don't think we
have much in common.

07:37.045 --> 07:39.749
Good heavens, Meg, you're
sprouting up like a weed!

07:39.818 --> 07:41.621
I know, she's
growing every day.

07:41.689 --> 07:43.524
Meg, you remember Dr. Hartman.

07:43.592 --> 07:46.734
Of course she does! I performed
her very first pelvic exam!

07:46.801 --> 07:50.007
Unless I'm confusing you
with someone else.

07:50.074 --> 07:52.580
Nope. That was...
that was you.

08:03.375 --> 08:04.777
Good evening, everyone.

08:04.845 --> 08:07.149
James Woods!

08:08.820 --> 08:11.258
Thank you for joining me
at my humble manor.

08:11.326 --> 08:14.599
I'd like to introduce you to
my lovely companion, Pricilla.

08:14.667 --> 08:15.769
Nice to meet you all.

08:15.837 --> 08:16.972
Who's he?

08:17.039 --> 08:18.106
James Woods.

08:18.174 --> 08:19.910
Oh, I thought
he was a shark.

08:19.978 --> 08:21.748
<i>No, he was a on a
show called Shark.</i>

08:21.816 --> 08:23.420
But he's made of wood?

08:23.488 --> 08:26.193
No, his last name is Woods,
but he's not made of wood.

08:26.260 --> 08:27.096
Nobody is.

08:28.833 --> 08:33.611
This truly is a night to
celebrate, especially for me.

08:33.679 --> 08:35.315
Hey, what's
going on here, Woods?

08:35.383 --> 08:37.620
The invitation said this
was a dinner in my honor.

08:37.688 --> 08:38.990
That's what mine said, too.

08:39.058 --> 08:40.827
Yeah, me, too!
Mine, too.
Same here!

08:40.895 --> 08:42.165
Where's the food?

08:42.233 --> 08:44.704
Well, actually,
this dinner honors all of you.

08:44.772 --> 08:46.408
Where should I begin?

08:46.475 --> 08:49.848
You see, recently I've become
a born-again Christian.

08:49.916 --> 08:53.124
Thanks to this
beautiful little angel.

08:53.192 --> 08:55.563
She came into my life
as if out of nowhere,

08:55.631 --> 08:58.069
enchanted me beyond
my wildest dreams,

08:58.136 --> 09:00.841
and opened my eyes
to the cleansing truth

09:00.909 --> 09:02.815
of Jesus Christ's love.

09:02.882 --> 09:05.052
No, honey, it was
always within you.

09:05.120 --> 09:06.421
I just helped you find it.

09:06.490 --> 09:09.663
Um... what does all this gay
stuff have to do with us?

09:09.730 --> 09:12.068
Well, the fact
of the matter is, I have wronged

09:12.136 --> 09:14.875
each and every
one of you in some way.

09:14.943 --> 09:18.850
And, since I am a man of God
now, I am truly repentant.

09:18.917 --> 09:21.657
So, I invited you
all here to make amends.

09:21.725 --> 09:23.495
And why the hell
should we trust you?

09:23.562 --> 09:25.801
Yeah, you've
been terrorizing
our family for years.

09:25.869 --> 09:29.241
I understand that there is some
healing to do here tonight,

09:29.308 --> 09:31.482
and I am prepared to be patient.

09:31.550 --> 09:34.722
Please, won't you just
give me a chance?

09:34.789 --> 09:37.227
And I promise you
won't be disappointed.

09:37.296 --> 09:40.035
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'll just go check on dinner.

09:40.069 --> 09:41.338
Oh, I'll help
you, sweetheart.

09:45.147 --> 09:46.883
This is all
very strange.

09:46.951 --> 09:48.787
I agree.
Something's not right.

09:48.856 --> 09:51.428
I don't know, maybe we
should give him a chance.

09:51.496 --> 09:53.266
Maybe he really is born again.

09:53.334 --> 09:54.670
Well, he could be.

09:54.737 --> 09:57.041
It all depends on what
his astrological sign is.

09:57.108 --> 10:00.050
Shut up. Shut up.
Shut up. Shut up. Shut up.

10:00.117 --> 10:01.887
I'm very intuitive
with these things.

10:01.955 --> 10:05.329
Maybe if I sit in his chair, I
can get a reading on his energy.

10:05.396 --> 10:08.301
I mean, if he's an Aquarius, a
rebirth would not be unexpected.

10:08.369 --> 10:09.872
That's enough,
Stephanie.

10:09.940 --> 10:11.810
You know, it's like
when I did Glenn's star chart...

10:17.389 --> 10:21.566
Did the-- did the cork hit me?

10:24.707 --> 10:26.977
My God.
She's dead.

10:27.045 --> 10:28.584
She's been shot!

10:30.389 --> 10:32.392
I can't help feeling
this would be sadder

10:32.459 --> 10:34.029
if she wasn't heavy.

10:39.462 --> 10:41.497
Oh, my God.
It was him!

10:41.565 --> 10:44.370
It was James Woods!
He killed Stephanie!

10:44.437 --> 10:47.245
Jeez, I knew he was crazy, but I
didn't think he was a murderer!

10:47.313 --> 10:49.751
Oh, he must've brought
us here to kill us all!

10:49.818 --> 10:51.489
Run! Run for your lives!

10:54.662 --> 10:55.830
Quick! We got to
get out of here!

11:00.978 --> 11:02.782
Come on,
get in the car!

11:21.225 --> 11:22.561
Oh, my God, Peter,
back it up!

11:22.628 --> 11:23.830
Oh, really, Lois?

11:23.897 --> 11:25.233
I thought I might
drive forward.

11:25.301 --> 11:27.040
I thought that-that might
be a fun thing to do.

11:27.107 --> 11:28.242
Stop fighting!

11:33.254 --> 11:35.659
Oh, my God! Quick, Peter,
get in the back!

11:46.085 --> 11:47.854
Oh, thank God.
We made it.

11:47.922 --> 11:49.692
Oh! Aah!

11:49.760 --> 11:51.129
Ow! My neck!

11:51.197 --> 11:53.100
You backed into me,
and-and now... Oh!

11:53.167 --> 11:54.973
Your back!

11:55.041 --> 11:57.946
And my back!
My back, yes! Oh!

12:02.356 --> 12:04.528
All right, it looks like
we're stuck here.

12:04.597 --> 12:07.402
Storm has flooded the causeway,
and the bridge is destroyed.

12:07.470 --> 12:09.872
For the moment,
there's no way out.

12:09.940 --> 12:11.174
<i>No Way Out. Great film.</i>

12:11.242 --> 12:12.812
Sean Young naked in the limo?

12:12.880 --> 12:14.016
What are we
gonna do?

12:14.084 --> 12:15.353
We can't just
stay here

12:15.421 --> 12:17.290
with James Woods lurking
somewhere in the house!

12:17.358 --> 12:19.095
All right, does anyone have
a cell phone?

12:20.665 --> 12:22.168
I'm not getting
any reception!

12:22.235 --> 12:23.707
Me neither!
No bars!

12:23.774 --> 12:25.077
It's all right.

12:25.144 --> 12:26.880
I'll put a message
in a bottle.

12:30.489 --> 12:32.760
Now... we wait.

12:32.828 --> 12:34.866
Look, he's got a land line
we can use!

12:34.935 --> 12:37.506
Oh, no. You know, I wouldn't
feel right about that.

12:37.574 --> 12:39.476
We're guests,
and it's long distance.

12:39.543 --> 12:40.712
Doesn't matter.

12:40.780 --> 12:42.115
The line's dead.

12:45.325 --> 12:46.627
Whoa, whoa, whoa, all right.

12:46.695 --> 12:48.932
Look, everybody but Chris,
just keep your pants on

12:49.000 --> 12:51.037
and let's figure a way
out of this.

12:51.104 --> 12:53.077
He's right. We just
got to stay calm.

12:53.145 --> 12:54.579
With a killer
in the house?!

12:54.648 --> 12:56.116
<i>Killer
in the house...!</i>

12:56.184 --> 12:58.255
Hey, guys,
has anybody seen James?

12:58.322 --> 13:00.560
Sweetheart, you may want
to sit down for this.

13:00.628 --> 13:02.933
Who want little tiny tacos?

13:03.001 --> 13:05.506
Ooh, little taco.
I'll have one of those.

13:05.574 --> 13:06.841
It's him!

13:06.909 --> 13:08.076
Sorry I took so long.

13:08.144 --> 13:09.647
I was going to the bathroom,

13:09.715 --> 13:11.820
and I just couldn't stop
looking at my penis,

13:11.887 --> 13:13.256
'cause it's, you know,
so fantastic.

13:13.324 --> 13:15.027
You're a monster...
Yeah, I heard it's fantastic.

13:15.095 --> 13:16.497
You're a monster, James Woods!

13:16.565 --> 13:19.036
You think you can just commit
murder and get away with it?!

13:19.104 --> 13:20.271
Quagmire loved that girl!

13:20.339 --> 13:21.376
Easy.

13:21.444 --> 13:22.680
Murder?

13:22.748 --> 13:23.949
Wha-What are you
talking about?

13:24.016 --> 13:26.286
You're going away
for a long time, pal.

13:26.354 --> 13:27.591
Jimmy, what
does he mean?

13:27.658 --> 13:29.628
Look, I honestly don't know
what's going on here.

13:29.696 --> 13:30.866
Oh, really?

13:30.933 --> 13:32.704
Well, maybe that dead pile
of cookie dough

13:32.772 --> 13:34.474
in the next room
will refresh your memory.

13:34.542 --> 13:35.710
What do you mean?

13:35.778 --> 13:38.081
There's nothing
in the next room.

13:43.262 --> 13:44.999
It's gone!

13:45.066 --> 13:47.170
Where is she, Woods?
What'd you do with the body?

13:47.237 --> 13:48.505
What body?

13:48.574 --> 13:50.112
You know,
maybe she wasn't dead.

13:50.180 --> 13:52.651
I'll admit it, I'm-I'm not great
with that stuff sometimes.

13:52.718 --> 13:54.621
All right, I don't know
what's happening here,

13:54.689 --> 13:56.293
but look, I'm a lot
of things.

13:56.360 --> 13:58.697
A member of Mensa,
a huge hit with the ladies,

13:58.765 --> 14:00.837
someone who, you know,
would have broken out bigger

14:00.904 --> 14:02.675
if he weren't so impossible
to work with.

14:02.742 --> 14:03.910
Right. But a murderer?

14:03.979 --> 14:06.014
I only just found God.

14:06.082 --> 14:08.385
Why would I jeopardize
my entrance into heaven?

14:08.453 --> 14:10.325
If I were you,
I'd keep your mouth shut

14:10.392 --> 14:11.660
till you talk to a lawyer.

14:11.729 --> 14:13.666
I didn't kill anybody!

14:16.506 --> 14:17.774
Oh my God.

14:17.842 --> 14:19.882
Is this what black people see
all the time?

14:25.027 --> 14:26.997
Look!

14:31.076 --> 14:32.511
He's dead.

14:32.579 --> 14:33.915
Oh, my God!

14:33.982 --> 14:35.183
Nice.

14:35.251 --> 14:36.619
Nobody touch the knife!

14:36.687 --> 14:38.492
There could be
fingerprints on it.

14:38.559 --> 14:40.797
So James Woods
murdered Stephanie,

14:40.865 --> 14:42.234
and then he
murdered himself.

14:42.302 --> 14:43.537
Criss-cross.

14:43.605 --> 14:45.006
No, Peter.
Don't you see?

14:45.074 --> 14:47.545
He didn't kill himself, and
he didn't kill Stephanie.

14:47.613 --> 14:48.951
What are you saying?

14:49.018 --> 14:51.756
I'm saying, James Woods
isn't the murderer.

14:51.824 --> 14:53.728
The murderer...

14:53.796 --> 14:55.565
is one of us!

14:57.070 --> 15:00.211
And someone ate the last
goat cheese tartlet.

15:01.916 --> 15:03.650
Now I hope
I die next.

15:11.826 --> 15:12.594
Okay, everyone,

15:12.641 --> 15:14.544
it's important that
we all stay calm.

15:14.612 --> 15:16.281
How are we supposed
to stay calm?!

15:16.349 --> 15:17.620
There's a killer
in the room!

15:17.687 --> 15:19.323
We all got to get out of here!

15:19.391 --> 15:20.425
We're all gonna die!

15:20.493 --> 15:22.396
Mr. Mayor,
pull yourself together!

15:23.734 --> 15:25.871
Wait a minute.
Joe, look!

15:36.566 --> 15:37.934
Oh, my God.

15:38.001 --> 15:39.771
Stephanie was
an accident.

15:39.839 --> 15:41.174
That's a way of putting it.

15:41.243 --> 15:42.544
What do you
mean, Joe?

15:42.612 --> 15:45.083
This gun was timed to fire
directly at that chair,

15:45.151 --> 15:46.722
where James Woods
would have been sitting.

15:46.790 --> 15:48.059
But he left,

15:48.126 --> 15:49.963
and Stephanie was
in the wrong place

15:50.030 --> 15:51.231
at the wrong time.

15:51.299 --> 15:52.768
So whoever the murderer is,

15:52.837 --> 15:55.610
they were after James Woods,
not Stephanie.

15:55.678 --> 15:57.548
The question is,

15:57.617 --> 16:00.086
who here wanted
James Woods dead?

16:06.435 --> 16:09.208
Let's look around and see
if we can find any more clues.

16:17.361 --> 16:20.066
Oh, my God.

16:21.905 --> 16:23.240
Brian, I feel like
everyone's wondering

16:23.307 --> 16:24.511
why I'm wearing shorts.

16:24.579 --> 16:25.580
Nobody's even
looking at you.

16:25.648 --> 16:26.817
That's what I mean.

16:26.885 --> 16:28.688
The fact that
no one has said anything

16:28.755 --> 16:30.858
makes it even more obvious
that everyone has noticed.

16:30.926 --> 16:32.195
Brian, look
what I found!

16:32.264 --> 16:33.432
Check it out!

16:33.499 --> 16:35.437
I'm a robot from outer space!

16:35.504 --> 16:36.639
Hang on. I'm coming down.

16:36.707 --> 16:38.877
Go, go, gadget skis!

16:43.892 --> 16:45.427
Uh-oh.

16:45.495 --> 16:48.600
All right, since it's my fault
that Joe got knocked out,

16:48.669 --> 16:51.875
it is now my responsibility
to take over the investigation.

16:51.943 --> 16:53.647
I-I don't know if
that actually follows.

16:53.715 --> 16:55.084
Oh, it does follow, Brian.

16:55.152 --> 16:58.189
Because I'm the one
with the giant magnifying glass.

16:58.257 --> 16:59.860
Is my eye big?
Yeah.

16:59.927 --> 17:01.197
Good.

17:01.265 --> 17:02.869
Good. That means progress.

17:02.936 --> 17:04.705
All right, let's-let's
figure out what we know here.

17:04.773 --> 17:06.978
The gun was clearly meant
to kill James Woods,

17:07.045 --> 17:08.847
but Stephanie got in the way.

17:08.916 --> 17:10.618
So the murderer had to improvise

17:10.685 --> 17:12.558
and finish the job
by stabbing him.

17:12.626 --> 17:15.464
Now who here had a motive
for wanting James Woods dead?

17:15.532 --> 17:17.736
Well, according
to James Woods, we all did.

17:17.804 --> 17:20.141
He brought us here
to make amends with us.

17:20.209 --> 17:22.882
But he wronged one of us
enough to want revenge.

17:22.950 --> 17:25.154
The question is, who?

17:25.222 --> 17:27.293
Well, I know one person
who could have.

17:27.360 --> 17:29.197
My partner Tom.

17:30.467 --> 17:31.871
All right, it's true.

17:31.939 --> 17:34.008
James Woods ruined my career!

17:34.076 --> 17:35.779
I originally wanted
to be an actor.

17:35.848 --> 17:38.351
<i>And I booked the lead role
in Nightmare On Elm Street.</i>

17:38.419 --> 17:39.855
But James Woods said,
"No, don't bother.

17:39.922 --> 17:41.293
Something else will come along."

17:41.361 --> 17:42.763
So I turned it down.

17:42.831 --> 17:45.469
And now this Robert Englund
is the talk of the town.

17:45.537 --> 17:47.273
That should be me
everyone's talking about!

17:47.341 --> 17:48.710
Was I angry?
Yes, of course!

17:48.777 --> 17:49.912
But I didn't kill him!

17:49.980 --> 17:51.049
What about Seamus?

17:51.117 --> 17:52.219
You hated James Woods.

17:52.287 --> 17:53.756
You told me so!

17:53.824 --> 17:57.596
Aye. He's the one
who made me what I am today.

17:59.002 --> 18:01.942
I wish you were a real,
live ornery sea captain.

18:02.010 --> 18:03.377
But he didn't
wish hard enough!

18:03.444 --> 18:04.881
It only worked
on me head!

18:04.949 --> 18:06.050
Oh, my God,
seriously?

18:06.118 --> 18:07.687
No. Actually,
I was a normal guy

18:07.755 --> 18:09.323
until one night,
we dropped acid together,

18:09.391 --> 18:10.963
and he thought
I was a steak.

18:11.031 --> 18:12.600
Grilled me,
ate me arms and legs.

18:12.668 --> 18:15.004
It was a whole thing.
But I'm not the killer!

18:15.072 --> 18:16.375
What about
the mayor?

18:16.443 --> 18:18.513
He could have killed him
and got himself off scot-free!

18:19.985 --> 18:21.755
He took the Twitter name
Mayor West,

18:21.823 --> 18:25.263
so now I have
to use Mayor underscore West.

18:25.331 --> 18:27.368
That rat-faced cracker!

18:27.436 --> 18:29.607
But you hated him,
too, Dr. Hartman.

18:29.675 --> 18:31.645
Sure, I hated him,
but so did Mort.

18:31.714 --> 18:32.947
I didn't kill him!

18:33.015 --> 18:34.184
Maybe it
was Diane.

18:35.555 --> 18:37.958
James Woods promised
to introduce me to Dan Rather.

18:38.026 --> 18:40.500
But instead, he introduced me
to Danny Bonaduce.

18:40.568 --> 18:43.406
I tell you, that guy looks
like a dog turning 30.

18:43.474 --> 18:45.177
But what about the old guy?

18:45.245 --> 18:47.782
I heard him complaining
about Woods in the dining room.

18:47.850 --> 18:49.087
That's true.

18:49.155 --> 18:51.994
He replaced my Cialis
with methamphetamines!

18:52.062 --> 18:53.130
Pedal faster!

18:53.197 --> 18:54.398
I can't go any faster!

18:54.465 --> 18:55.533
Where you
going, kids?

18:55.601 --> 18:57.204
Hey, I just want
to talk to you.

18:57.272 --> 18:58.743
Why don't you come
over to my place

18:58.811 --> 19:00.814
for a glass of wine and
a couple of fruit pies,

19:00.882 --> 19:02.651
and then we can go
in the back room

19:02.719 --> 19:03.887
and play crazy snake.
Hee-hee-hee!

19:03.954 --> 19:05.757
And what about Quagmire?

19:05.825 --> 19:08.198
Fine! So he stole
Cheryl Tiegs from me!

19:08.267 --> 19:09.635
He ruined your TV pilot!

19:09.702 --> 19:11.739
Go to hell! I backed out
of that project willingly.

19:11.807 --> 19:13.041
Oh, yeah, that's what
every hack says.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.212
You know, Brian...
I'm telling you...

19:32.288 --> 19:34.058
Eh. My secret
room's bigger.

19:34.126 --> 19:35.895
Mine's smaller.

19:38.103 --> 19:39.305
All right, stand back.

19:39.373 --> 19:41.209
This could be dangerous.

19:43.716 --> 19:45.218
Oh, laundry room.

19:45.286 --> 19:47.124
Laundry room, everybody.

19:54.407 --> 19:56.379
Oh, see, here we go.

20:24.412 --> 20:26.149
Aha!

20:26.217 --> 20:28.355
James Woods made a list
of all his misdeeds

20:28.422 --> 20:29.725
so he could make amends.

20:29.792 --> 20:31.561
Bonnie, he punched you
in the throat,

20:31.629 --> 20:33.465
and that's why
you sound like that?

20:33.532 --> 20:37.142
<i>No, he punched me in the throat
because I sound like this.</i>

20:37.210 --> 20:38.544
And Consuela, he...

20:38.612 --> 20:40.283
Actually, I can't read
his handwriting here.

20:40.350 --> 20:41.518
What-what happened?

20:41.586 --> 20:43.857
One day, I bring
my nephew to work,

20:43.924 --> 20:47.868
and he molest my nephew,
and my nephew-- he only 14,

20:47.935 --> 20:52.043
and he cry, and then,
he shoot himself in the face.

20:52.110 --> 20:54.149
What are all these?

20:54.217 --> 20:56.988
God, there are tons
of OxyContin bottles in here.

20:57.056 --> 20:59.294
All prescribed to James Woods.

20:59.362 --> 21:01.497
And all from Goldman's Pharmacy.

21:01.565 --> 21:03.034
What's that
all about, Goldman?

21:03.102 --> 21:04.908
I don't know what
you're talking about.

21:04.975 --> 21:08.014
James Woods never bought
anything in my pharmacy. Ever.

21:08.082 --> 21:09.517
Yes, he did.

21:09.585 --> 21:12.256
Says here he talked Muriel
into selling him OxyContin

21:12.324 --> 21:13.995
for him
and his 19-year-old girlfriend.

21:14.063 --> 21:15.433
This went on for weeks,

21:15.501 --> 21:17.136
but then she started
to have misgivings

21:17.204 --> 21:18.706
and threatened to cut him off.

21:18.774 --> 21:20.210
But he wouldn't let her.

21:20.277 --> 21:23.285
He threatened to blackmail her
by turning her in to the Feds.

21:23.353 --> 21:25.323
Sounds like
a pretty good motive to me.

21:25.391 --> 21:27.027
No! No, it's not true!

21:27.095 --> 21:28.797
I would never kill anybody,
never!

21:28.866 --> 21:30.767
And I am not saying another word

21:30.835 --> 21:32.573
until I talk to my lawyer,
because...

21:32.641 --> 21:33.977
Why is he wearing shorts?

21:34.044 --> 21:35.881
Oh, my God,
I told you!

21:35.948 --> 21:38.086
Muriel, just surrender quietly.

21:38.154 --> 21:40.290
It'll be easier
for us all if you...

21:44.870 --> 21:46.373
She's gone!

21:54.927 --> 21:56.029
We lost her.

21:56.096 --> 21:57.031
Well, as long as there's

21:57.098 --> 21:58.066
a murderer on the loose,

21:58.134 --> 21:59.501
none of us are safe.

21:59.569 --> 22:01.374
All right, let's split up
and search the house.

22:01.442 --> 22:02.744
I'll go with Lois.

22:02.812 --> 22:04.548
Chris, you check the basement
with Herbert.

22:05.785 --> 22:07.287
Meg, you go
with Brian and Stewie.

22:07.355 --> 22:09.058
Uh, no,
she-she can't.

22:09.125 --> 22:10.261
Yeah, uh,
she can't.

22:10.329 --> 22:12.869
We-we-we were gonna
use this time, uh...

22:12.936 --> 22:15.174
to figure out what to get
you for your birthday.

22:15.242 --> 22:16.943
Ooh, ah, okay.
Oh, yeah, no, you guys go.

22:17.012 --> 22:18.146
You guys-- ooh,
now I'm excited.

22:18.214 --> 22:19.450
Um, okay, um, Meg,

22:19.518 --> 22:21.189
you go with Carl.
Sorry, Carl.

22:21.257 --> 22:22.458
Tom and Diane,
you're a team.

22:22.526 --> 22:24.195
Quagmire and Bonnie,
you're a team.

22:24.264 --> 22:27.135
Um... Seamus and Dr. Hartman?
That-that could be funny.

22:27.203 --> 22:28.938
Don't usually see
the two of you together.

22:29.006 --> 22:31.045
Uh, Derek and Jillian,
you guys take the attic.

22:31.113 --> 22:32.849
Joe and Priscilla
are still passed out,

22:32.917 --> 22:34.285
so they'll be
the unconscious team.

22:34.353 --> 22:37.125
And that leaves
one three-person team

22:37.192 --> 22:39.397
of Mort, Consuela,
and Mayor West.

22:39.464 --> 22:41.604
All right. Let's do this.

22:44.443 --> 22:46.780
So, uh...

22:46.848 --> 22:48.251
You guys like
to party?

22:48.319 --> 22:49.422
No!

22:49.489 --> 22:51.125
Oh, no.

22:51.193 --> 22:53.564
Oh, my God, what a
couple of squares.

22:53.633 --> 22:55.134
Squaresville,
I tell ya!

23:11.220 --> 23:12.688
What are we supposed
to be doing again?

23:12.756 --> 23:14.625
We're looking
for Muriel Goldman, honey.

23:24.451 --> 23:26.420
Hello?

23:26.488 --> 23:28.058
Is anybody up here?

23:42.425 --> 23:45.599
Hey, maybe it was that cat
who was the murderer.

23:45.667 --> 23:46.835
Let me ask him.

23:46.902 --> 23:49.642
Meow, meow, meow?
Meow-meow-meow-meow?

23:49.710 --> 23:51.781
We don't all talk like that.

23:51.849 --> 23:53.384
I happen to be a professor.

23:53.452 --> 23:54.854
Our apologies, sir.

23:54.921 --> 23:56.590
I should imagine so.

23:56.660 --> 23:58.830
Now if you'll excuse me,
I have papers to correct.

24:03.910 --> 24:06.917
Chris, I'm worried, with
this killer on the loose.

24:06.985 --> 24:10.391
If I should die, I-I
just want you to know

24:10.459 --> 24:12.495
that they might
find some things.

24:12.564 --> 24:16.373
Strange things.

24:16.441 --> 24:18.176
Um... okay.

24:18.244 --> 24:19.881
And there's gonna
be a lot of talk.

24:19.949 --> 24:21.351
Nasty talk.

24:21.419 --> 24:23.889
And I just want you
to know, from me,

24:23.957 --> 24:26.530
it's all gonna be
out of context.

24:26.598 --> 24:28.401
I don't know
what that means.

24:28.468 --> 24:31.641
It means, if I die, you
got to burn my house down!

24:37.959 --> 24:39.728
Muriel?

24:39.796 --> 24:41.931
Oh, yeah, like she's going
to answer you, Tom.

24:41.999 --> 24:43.936
And here we go
with the attitude.

24:44.004 --> 24:45.207
This is why
you're single.

24:45.275 --> 24:46.978
Oh, so I'm not
supposed to point out

24:47.045 --> 24:48.314
when you do
something stupid?

24:48.382 --> 24:50.252
You hear that? You hear
that tone you're using?

24:50.320 --> 24:51.822
That's penis repellent
right there.

24:57.670 --> 24:59.172
Careful.

24:59.240 --> 25:01.277
She could be hiding behind
any one of these statues.

25:02.915 --> 25:06.124
Muriel, this is Tom Tucker
from the Channel Five news.

25:06.191 --> 25:07.660
Perhaps you'd like
an autograph.

25:07.728 --> 25:09.398
Oh, for God's sakes.
Do you hear yourself?

25:09.465 --> 25:10.433
There it is.

25:11.669 --> 25:13.005
Knock it off!

25:14.445 --> 25:15.813
Hey, wait a minute.

25:15.881 --> 25:17.651
Doesn't feel like
there's any wall here.

25:25.805 --> 25:28.208
What do you
think's in there?

25:28.276 --> 25:30.080
I don't know.
Looks scary.

25:30.147 --> 25:31.883
What do you
think, Ollie?

25:31.951 --> 25:33.188
I miss Ollie.

25:33.255 --> 25:34.892
I better take a look.

25:34.960 --> 25:36.830
No. I'll go first.

25:38.834 --> 25:41.038
Do you see anything?

25:41.106 --> 25:43.512
No, it's-it's
too dark.

25:45.884 --> 25:48.523
Tom? Tom!

25:51.597 --> 25:53.202
Oh, sweet.
A pool table.

25:53.270 --> 25:55.072
Let's see if we can
find some cues.

26:04.696 --> 26:05.731
What is it?!

26:05.798 --> 26:07.935
Whew. It's okay.

26:08.003 --> 26:10.308
<i>It's just the stuffed bear
from The Great Outdoors.</i>

26:10.376 --> 26:11.846
<i>Did you see
The Great Outdoors?</i>

26:11.914 --> 26:13.349
No.
You suck.

26:13.417 --> 26:15.287
Hey, I found the pool cues!

26:22.072 --> 26:22.973
Meg?

26:24.944 --> 26:26.546
Looks like I'm all alone.

26:26.614 --> 26:28.050
Well, hey, that's all right.

26:28.117 --> 26:29.152
I watch a lot of movies.

26:29.220 --> 26:31.426
I can just use my imagination.

26:31.493 --> 26:32.628
Hi, Carl.

26:32.697 --> 26:33.898
Hey, bear.

26:33.966 --> 26:35.567
So, um, in the
bear world,

26:35.635 --> 26:38.708
are, like, pandas your version
of interracial children?

26:38.775 --> 26:41.215
Yeah. Pandas aren't
something I agree with.

26:41.283 --> 26:42.351
They're cute,
though, right?

26:42.418 --> 26:44.121
Just when they're babies.

26:55.983 --> 26:57.753
Boy, it's really
raining hard.

26:57.820 --> 26:59.959
Yeah, well,
we needed it.

27:00.027 --> 27:01.262
What?

27:01.330 --> 27:03.100
Peter, we've been
married a long time.

27:03.168 --> 27:05.371
Why do I still get "guy in
an elevator" small talk?

27:05.439 --> 27:07.643
I don't know. You're the one
talking about the weather.

27:07.711 --> 27:09.047
So...

27:09.114 --> 27:11.854
Looking forward
to the weekend?

27:19.307 --> 27:20.676
It's okay.
It's just us.

27:20.744 --> 27:23.448
Oh, Quagmire, Bonnie,
you scared us.

27:23.515 --> 27:25.586
Have you seen
any sign of Muriel?

27:25.654 --> 27:27.123
Oh, why didn't I
think of this before?

27:27.191 --> 27:29.663
I should just check the "Find
A Jew" app on my phone.

27:29.731 --> 27:32.871
Huh. There's just
two big clusters

27:32.939 --> 27:34.807
on each side of the country.

27:34.875 --> 27:36.979
No, look.
There's one down south.

27:37.047 --> 27:38.250
Ah, they got him.

27:46.636 --> 27:48.308
Okay, um...

27:52.151 --> 27:53.652
<i>Oh, uh, Lost in Space.</i>

27:53.720 --> 27:55.456
Yup, okay. Um...

27:58.765 --> 28:00.135
<i>Oh, uh, uh, that's
Dick Van Dyke.</i>

28:00.203 --> 28:01.337
Okay, um...

28:01.405 --> 28:03.041
Oh, okay,
I-I-I got one, um...

28:09.525 --> 28:10.693
I have no idea.

28:10.761 --> 28:13.834
в™Є Linda Evans
and John Forsythe в™Є

28:13.901 --> 28:16.606
в™Є They're coming down
big, long stairs в™Є

28:16.677 --> 28:19.114
в™Є Come on, Brian,
you know this в™Є

28:19.182 --> 28:20.584
в™Є We're all rich в™Є

28:20.651 --> 28:25.227
в™Є And we're all
at least in our late 50s в™Є

28:25.294 --> 28:27.233
в™Є Think Joan Collins в™Є

28:28.972 --> 28:29.973
в™Є Come on, Brian,
you know this в™Є

28:31.375 --> 28:32.209
в™Є It's the middle
trumpet part в™Є

28:33.680 --> 28:35.885
в™Є It was a pretty big deal
for Diahann Carroll в™Є

28:35.954 --> 28:38.191
в™Є To play a rich, black woman
in the 80s. в™Є

28:38.259 --> 28:39.929
Come on, Bri. Right?
Y-You don't know this?

28:39.997 --> 28:41.399
<i>Uh, Falcon Crest?</i>

28:41.467 --> 28:43.169
<i>Oh, it's "Dinasty"!</i>

28:43.237 --> 28:45.207
Oh. Yeah, I-I
didn't watch that.

28:54.062 --> 28:55.833
Oh, my God!

28:59.777 --> 29:01.846
Oh, my God, Muriel!

29:01.914 --> 29:03.484
My sweet Muriel!

29:03.552 --> 29:06.726
She was so young.
She was so beauti--

29:06.794 --> 29:08.496
She was so genero--

29:08.564 --> 29:10.835
Uh, we were married.

29:10.903 --> 29:14.076
Look! This is the same knife
that killed James Woods.

29:14.143 --> 29:15.481
Oh, my God!

29:15.549 --> 29:17.752
Then Muriel wasn't the killer.

29:17.821 --> 29:19.790
Well, then, who is?

29:19.858 --> 29:21.894
I don't know,
but one thing's for sure.

29:21.962 --> 29:24.636
If we don't find out
before this storm lets up,

29:24.703 --> 29:27.375
we're all gonna be dead
by morning.

29:41.969 --> 29:43.808
All right, if we're going
to make it out alive,

29:43.876 --> 29:45.311
we got to stick
together from now on.

29:45.379 --> 29:47.048
Is everyone here?

29:47.116 --> 29:48.217
Wait a minute, wait.
Where's Meg?

29:48.285 --> 29:49.420
And where's Tom Tucker?

29:49.488 --> 29:50.589
Right here!

29:50.657 --> 29:52.258
Oh, my God!
What happened?

29:52.326 --> 29:53.630
I fell through a trapdoor

29:53.698 --> 29:55.100
that led to
an underground passageway.

29:55.168 --> 29:56.737
So I followed it,
and it led me

29:56.805 --> 29:58.006
to a hatch over there
in the parlor.

29:58.074 --> 29:59.443
The same thing
happened to me.

29:59.511 --> 30:00.578
But with
a moustache.

30:00.647 --> 30:01.982
Hey, Peter,
look at this.

30:02.050 --> 30:04.389
I'm getting a faint signal
on my cell phone.

30:04.457 --> 30:05.458
Really?

30:05.526 --> 30:06.661
Oh, my god, is that...

30:06.729 --> 30:09.300
Are you holding up
the whole Hollywood sign?

30:09.368 --> 30:10.402
No, no, no, no.

30:10.470 --> 30:12.276
The sign was way
in the background.

30:12.344 --> 30:14.380
I was standing in the
foreground gng like this

30:14.448 --> 30:15.583
when Jillian took the picture,

30:15.651 --> 30:17.252
so by forced perspective,

30:17.320 --> 30:19.124
it looks like I'm holding
up the whole sign.

30:19.192 --> 30:21.528
I don't believe you.
I think you are a god.

30:21.596 --> 30:23.802
And I will die for
you or kill others.

30:23.870 --> 30:25.206
Damn it.
The signal's gone.

30:25.273 --> 30:27.275
If I can get up
to the roof or something,

30:27.343 --> 30:29.781
maybe I can get a stronger
signal and call the police.

30:29.849 --> 30:32.455
Okay. And I will skin
this dog in your honor.

30:32.523 --> 30:33.824
Please don't.
As you wish.

30:33.893 --> 30:35.864
Do you really think
it could work, Derek?

30:35.931 --> 30:37.600
There's only one
way to find out.

30:37.667 --> 30:39.003
I'll be back.

30:40.941 --> 30:43.081
All right, nobody leaves
this room until he gets back.

30:43.149 --> 30:44.951
Wait a minute.

30:45.019 --> 30:46.990
Something's not right here.

30:47.058 --> 30:49.528
We're short one vagina
in this room.

30:49.595 --> 30:51.099
Oh, my God!

30:51.167 --> 30:52.436
Priscilla's gone!

30:56.412 --> 30:58.248
Th-That's impossible.

30:58.316 --> 31:00.253
She was still passed out
on the couch when we left.

31:01.492 --> 31:02.994
What the hell happened?

31:03.062 --> 31:04.665
Joe! You're okay!

31:04.733 --> 31:06.435
Yeah, I'm fine.
What's going on?

31:06.503 --> 31:08.640
What's going on is,
Priscilla's the murderer!

31:08.708 --> 31:09.909
Wait a second.
We don't know that.

31:09.980 --> 31:11.916
Well, she was by herself
this whole time!

31:11.984 --> 31:13.285
Yes, but she was unconscious!

31:13.354 --> 31:15.256
She could've come to
and killed Muriel!

31:15.325 --> 31:17.362
This is all speculation!
We don't know she's the killer!

31:17.430 --> 31:18.498
Yeah, besides, she's hot!

31:18.564 --> 31:19.834
Hot chicks are never crazy!

31:19.902 --> 31:21.371
Derek lifted
up the Hollywood sign.

31:25.747 --> 31:28.086
He did, too! I
saw the picture!

32:16.903 --> 32:18.406
Come on.

32:28.430 --> 32:30.066
Yes!

32:33.241 --> 32:34.543
Hey.

32:34.611 --> 32:36.180
What are you doing up here?

32:36.248 --> 32:37.452
Wait a minute.

32:37.520 --> 32:39.122
What the hell is this?

32:39.190 --> 32:41.527
Oh, my God! It's you!

32:41.594 --> 32:44.267
The man or woman
who's been killing everybody!

32:44.335 --> 32:46.004
Stay back. Stay back.

32:56.364 --> 32:57.799
It came from over there!

33:01.041 --> 33:02.543
Dear God!

33:05.083 --> 33:06.554
He's dead.

33:06.622 --> 33:08.625
Do you think he
slipped off the roof?

33:08.693 --> 33:11.030
Maybe. But he was dead
before the fall.

33:11.098 --> 33:14.304
Look at this-- he's
been hit on the head
by a blunt object.

33:14.372 --> 33:17.279
Oh, my God, no, Derek!

33:17.347 --> 33:19.518
Oh, Jillian,
I'm so sorry.

33:19.585 --> 33:20.986
Hey, can you
grab his phone?

33:21.053 --> 33:22.589
I want to prove
something to these guys.

33:31.608 --> 33:32.942
I-I-It's Priscilla.

33:33.011 --> 33:34.449
I-I mean, it's
got to be Priscilla.

33:34.517 --> 33:35.886
She's the only one
who's not here.

33:35.953 --> 33:36.988
Look, maybe, maybe not.

33:37.056 --> 33:38.190
We thought
Muriel was the killer,

33:38.258 --> 33:39.459
and look how that turned out.

33:39.527 --> 33:40.830
We have no proof of anything.

33:40.898 --> 33:42.767
Is this the latest
you've ever stayed up?

33:42.835 --> 33:44.305
<i>It's the latest
I've ever stayed up.</i>

33:44.373 --> 33:45.775
Oh, no!

33:45.843 --> 33:48.614
Someone's taken
Mr. Woods' Golden Globe!

33:51.688 --> 33:54.729
She's right! There was
a Golden Globe award
here, and it's gone.

33:54.797 --> 33:57.435
I think we may
have identified
our blunt object.

33:57.503 --> 33:59.874
So all we have to do
is find that Golden Globe

33:59.943 --> 34:02.046
and we'll have
our murder weapon--
and if we're lucky,

34:02.114 --> 34:03.953
it may just mean
we'll have our killer.

34:04.020 --> 34:06.390
All right, from
this moment forward,

34:06.458 --> 34:08.194
nobody leaves the group.

34:08.262 --> 34:09.397
Joe's right.
Everyone huddle up.

34:11.904 --> 34:13.775
Good. Now, we're gonna
search the house,

34:13.843 --> 34:15.412
and we're gonna move as one.

34:15.480 --> 34:16.815
Anyone who separates
from the group

34:16.883 --> 34:18.651
we will assume to be the killer.

34:18.719 --> 34:19.753
All clear?

34:19.821 --> 34:21.458
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

34:21.526 --> 34:22.493
All right.

34:22.561 --> 34:23.597
Let's do this!

34:34.257 --> 34:35.726
Oh, boy, we got
a problem here.

34:35.794 --> 34:37.196
All right,
on the count of three.

34:37.263 --> 34:38.867
One, two...

34:38.935 --> 34:40.169
three!

34:40.237 --> 34:41.271
Thanks, guys.

34:44.081 --> 34:47.153
Stop it, Peter.

34:47.221 --> 34:48.488
Peter, knock it off!

34:48.556 --> 34:49.858
Okay, Jew. Joe.

34:49.926 --> 34:51.395
Shut up!
I'm not Jewish!

34:51.465 --> 34:54.303
<i>Well, I think we've
learned a little something</i>

34:54.371 --> 34:57.410
about our friendly
neighborhood
policeman today.

34:57.478 --> 35:00.851
All right, we got to search
every one of these rooms.

35:00.919 --> 35:02.190
We'll start with Quagmire's.

35:06.266 --> 35:08.236
Oh, my God!

35:08.305 --> 35:10.207
Are those
Stephanie's underpants?

35:10.276 --> 35:11.245
Oh, God.

35:11.313 --> 35:12.614
They're huge!

35:12.683 --> 35:15.387
Looks like the crotch got
chewed on by a walrus mouth.

35:15.454 --> 35:17.590
Look, it's got flowers!

35:17.658 --> 35:18.927
I mean, why bother?

35:18.995 --> 35:20.230
Who's gonna see 'em?

35:20.298 --> 35:22.937
Maybe someone in space.

35:24.609 --> 35:27.080
Come on, guys, can't we all
just be glad she's dead?

35:37.573 --> 35:39.409
<i>Whose room is this?</i>

35:39.477 --> 35:40.914
It's, uh, my room.

35:40.981 --> 35:43.487
You travel with a giant
poster of yourself?

35:43.555 --> 35:46.759
Yes. It helps me get to sleep,
knowing that Big Tom Tucker

35:46.828 --> 35:49.099
is keeping a watchful eye out
for nocturnal intruders.

35:49.166 --> 35:50.771
What a ridiculous
man you are.

35:50.839 --> 35:53.210
Look, I didn't know my room
was gonna be scrutinized.

35:53.277 --> 35:55.548
I-If you don't like it,
let's get out of here.

35:55.616 --> 35:57.819
Not till we've
searched the place.

36:10.553 --> 36:12.891
You guys?

36:16.664 --> 36:18.269
Oh, my God!

36:20.140 --> 36:24.015
Well, well, I think
we've found our killer.

36:24.082 --> 36:25.919
Oh, now, now, wait a minute,
that's not mine!

36:25.986 --> 36:28.394
I suppose it crawled under
your bed all by itself.

36:28.462 --> 36:29.463
Well, maybe it did.

36:29.530 --> 36:30.665
I didn't murder anybody.

36:30.732 --> 36:32.469
Tell it to Mike Judge.

36:32.536 --> 36:34.407
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
uh, this is crazy,

36:34.475 --> 36:35.609
Wh-What about Priscilla?

36:35.677 --> 36:37.313
We have no idea
where she is.

36:37.382 --> 36:38.650
She could've planted that there.

36:38.718 --> 36:39.988
Well, uh...

36:40.056 --> 36:42.760
I suppose it's possible.

36:42.827 --> 36:44.964
What the hell?

36:45.031 --> 36:47.304
Aw, dang it, I got a nosebleed.

36:47.372 --> 36:49.710
No, you don't.

36:54.321 --> 36:55.956
Peter, give me a boost.

37:04.880 --> 37:07.386
You're going
to jail, Tucker.

37:07.453 --> 37:09.491
Like hell I am!
You're not taking
me anywhere,

37:09.559 --> 37:10.794
you podunk,
Quahog redneck cop!

37:10.862 --> 37:13.130
Not you or anyone else
in this damn town!

37:13.197 --> 37:14.935
I'm not going to jail!

37:16.441 --> 37:18.176
After him!

37:34.515 --> 37:35.720
Give it up, Tucker!

37:35.787 --> 37:36.955
Make me, Swanson!

37:48.917 --> 37:50.854
Damn, he's slippery.

37:50.921 --> 37:52.624
You guys give up?

37:52.692 --> 37:54.831
What do we do?
Wait a minute,
wait a minute, guys!

37:54.900 --> 37:56.635
I got an idea.

37:56.703 --> 37:59.041
Shoot.
What if half of us
go around one side of the table,

37:59.108 --> 38:00.679
and the other half
go around the other side,

38:00.746 --> 38:02.816
and then we won't have
to chase him around in circles.

38:02.884 --> 38:04.254
Damn, that's
awfully risky.

38:04.321 --> 38:07.996
It sure is, but at this point
I'm willing to try anything.

38:09.298 --> 38:11.401
All right.
Let's do it!

38:12.739 --> 38:14.610
It worked!

38:14.678 --> 38:16.614
Let me go!

38:16.682 --> 38:18.419
Let me go,
you bastards!

38:18.487 --> 38:20.090
You're all gonna
pay for this!

38:21.660 --> 38:24.434
Just for that, when the movie
of this story comes out,

38:24.502 --> 38:26.572
I'm gonna make sure
Adrian Brody plays you.

38:26.639 --> 38:29.378
I guess that means you
don't want anyone to see it.

38:31.117 --> 38:33.088
Okay. All right.

39:01.825 --> 39:05.131
Thanks a lot for
your help, boys.

39:11.646 --> 39:13.516
You know, despite
all the craziness
this weekend,

39:13.584 --> 39:17.358
I feel like a lot of people
were looking at me like
I was really attractive.

39:17.426 --> 39:20.264
Which makes me think
that I'm gonna grow up
to be good-looking.

39:20.332 --> 39:21.570
What part of
that statement

39:21.638 --> 39:23.507
is supposed to lure me
into a conversation?

39:23.575 --> 39:26.847
I talk to you about
wet tennis balls.

39:26.916 --> 39:28.552
Oh, come on!

39:28.620 --> 39:30.154
We're in a fight!

39:31.728 --> 39:34.767
Lois, are any of my Hot Wheels
in the bath... L-Lois?

39:34.835 --> 39:36.271
Lois? Lois?

39:36.338 --> 39:38.977
Lois, are any of my Hot Wheels
in the bathroom?

39:39.045 --> 39:40.614
No, I put 'em all in your bag.

39:40.682 --> 39:42.451
Okay, well, I don't
see the fire engine,

39:42.519 --> 39:46.695
but I guess we'll just find out
when we get home, won't we?

39:46.763 --> 39:48.999
I'll see you in the car.

39:53.880 --> 39:55.616
Hi, Diane.

39:55.684 --> 39:57.086
Oh, hi, Lois.

39:57.154 --> 39:58.489
How you doing?

39:58.557 --> 40:01.029
I just thought I'd
make sure you were okay.

40:01.098 --> 40:02.969
Oh, I'm managing.

40:03.036 --> 40:05.005
It's just...
so hard to believe

40:05.073 --> 40:07.209
you can work with someone
for 15 years

40:07.277 --> 40:09.615
and yet have no idea
who they really are

40:09.683 --> 40:11.052
or what they're capable of.

40:11.120 --> 40:12.154
Oh, I know.

40:12.222 --> 40:13.625
And I'm sorry.

40:13.693 --> 40:15.563
So, what happens now?

40:15.630 --> 40:17.767
Will you just anchor
the news by yourself?

40:17.835 --> 40:19.774
I suppose, for the time being.

40:19.842 --> 40:22.112
Well, that's kind of
exciting, right?

40:22.179 --> 40:23.915
You sound
like my mother.

40:23.983 --> 40:25.353
She actually

40:25.421 --> 40:27.858
bought me this blouse
for my first solo broadcast.

40:27.925 --> 40:29.597
I guess that's sweet, huh?

40:29.664 --> 40:31.301
She... uh...

40:31.369 --> 40:33.272
I'm sorry, I don't understand.

40:33.340 --> 40:34.408
What do you mean?

40:34.475 --> 40:36.045
I mean, how could she have known

40:36.112 --> 40:37.448
you'd be anchoring alone?

40:37.516 --> 40:39.988
I mean, none of this
happened until...

40:48.009 --> 40:51.415
Gosh, I, uh, you know,
I think I'd better, uh...

40:51.483 --> 40:54.289
go make sure Peter
has his, uh...

40:54.356 --> 40:55.658
fire engine.

40:55.725 --> 40:56.726
Oh, really?

40:56.794 --> 40:58.632
But I was enjoying our talk.

40:58.700 --> 41:01.239
Oh, no, I... so was I,
but, you know,

41:01.307 --> 41:03.175
I've, really,
I should...
I should go.

41:03.243 --> 41:05.514
No. I don't think so.

41:05.583 --> 41:07.220
Oh, my God.

41:07.287 --> 41:09.256
<i>Oh, my God, it was you.</i>

41:09.324 --> 41:10.894
You're the killer!

41:10.962 --> 41:12.297
Very clever, Lois.

41:12.365 --> 41:14.468
You shouldn't have stopped
to say hi to me.

41:14.536 --> 41:15.837
You would've lived longer.

41:15.905 --> 41:18.546
God, why do I ever try to
be friends with other women?

41:18.614 --> 41:19.748
But, Diane, why?

41:19.816 --> 41:22.287
How could you do all
these horrible things?

41:22.355 --> 41:24.927
Well, I suppose it all
really began a year ago

41:24.995 --> 41:26.732
when James Woods and I met

41:26.800 --> 41:28.938
<i>at a press event
and began seeing each other.</i>

41:36.691 --> 41:39.261
<i>We both valued
our privacy, however,</i>

41:39.329 --> 41:42.569
<i>so we agreed to keep it
a secret from the media.</i>

41:48.184 --> 41:51.825
<i>Everything in my life
was wonderful.</i>

41:51.893 --> 41:54.396
<i>But then a few months ago,
I turned 40.</i>

41:54.464 --> 41:56.704
Surprise!

41:56.771 --> 41:58.507
<i>It was hard for me
to begin with,</i>

41:58.576 --> 42:01.880
<i>but it got worse when,
not so coincidentally,</i>

42:01.948 --> 42:04.119
<i>Tom began pushing
Channel Five News to replace me</i>

42:04.187 --> 42:06.226
<i>with a fresh, young face,</i>

42:06.294 --> 42:07.894
<i>and he succeeded.</i>

42:07.962 --> 42:11.603
<i>Three weeks from now,
I'll be off the air.</i>

42:11.671 --> 42:15.547
<i>Well, apparently,
all men think the same way,</i>

42:15.615 --> 42:18.120
<i>because around the same time,</i>

42:18.187 --> 42:21.193
<i>James dumped me.</i>

42:21.261 --> 42:24.068
<i>I watched my career
and my love life crumble,</i>

42:24.136 --> 42:26.441
<i>and I wasn't gonna just
stand by and take it.</i>

42:26.509 --> 42:28.378
<i>That's when I had
the good fortune</i>

42:28.446 --> 42:31.451
<i>to meet a young news intern
named Priscilla.</i>

42:31.519 --> 42:34.125
<i>She was so anxious to get
into the reporting business</i>

42:34.194 --> 42:37.098
<i>and would have done anything
to get on my good side.</i>

42:37.166 --> 42:39.003
<i>So I seized the moment.</i>

42:39.071 --> 42:42.109
<i>I paid her off to seduce
James Woods and reel him</i>

42:42.177 --> 42:44.951
<i>into a relationship
like a fish on a line.</i>

42:45.019 --> 42:47.389
<i>I knew a hot, young woman
like Priscilla</i>

42:47.457 --> 42:50.429
<i>could manipulate him
into doing anything I wanted.</i>

42:50.497 --> 42:52.100
<i>At my direction,
she persuaded him</i>

42:52.167 --> 42:54.272
<i>to become
a born-again Christian,</i>

42:54.340 --> 42:56.779
<i>and instilled him with
the drive to bring together</i>

42:56.847 --> 42:58.782
<i>all the people he'd wronged.</i>

42:58.850 --> 43:01.789
<i>That's how this weekend
came to pass.</i>

43:01.857 --> 43:05.665
<i>Of course, Priscilla knew
nothing of my real intentions,</i>

43:05.733 --> 43:08.271
<i>but she played the part
beautifully, nonetheless.</i>

43:08.339 --> 43:10.342
There's no way
she could have known

43:10.410 --> 43:13.551
I planned to kill James Woods
and frame Tom Tucker,

43:13.619 --> 43:15.488
thereby destroying
the two people

43:15.557 --> 43:18.262
who cast me aside
and ruined my life.

43:18.329 --> 43:20.299
Oh, my God...

43:20.368 --> 43:21.838
you're 40?

43:21.906 --> 43:23.976
Yes. I'm 40.

43:24.044 --> 43:26.315
But then why did
you kill the others?

43:26.383 --> 43:28.619
It was all supposed
to go so smoothly.

43:28.687 --> 43:30.357
<i>The hidden gun goes off,</i>

43:30.425 --> 43:32.597
<i>kills James Woods,
and at the first opportunity,</i>

43:32.665 --> 43:35.971
<i>I retrieve the gun
and plant it in Tom's bag.</i>

43:36.039 --> 43:37.407
<i>James Woods is dead,</i>

43:37.475 --> 43:39.879
<i>Tom goes to prison--
nice and easy.</i>

43:39.947 --> 43:41.853
<i>But Stephanie got in the way.</i>

43:41.920 --> 43:44.190
<i>She was in James' chair
at the wrong time.</i>

43:44.258 --> 43:45.460
<i>And when I realized</i>

43:45.528 --> 43:47.732
<i>my mistake,
I had to improvise.</i>

43:47.800 --> 43:50.740
<i>The power outage provided
a perfect cover.</i>

43:50.808 --> 43:54.582
<i>I grabbed the knife off the
dinner table and stabbed him.</i>

43:54.650 --> 43:57.020
<i>But as Joe pointed out,
there were fingerprints.</i>

43:57.088 --> 43:58.790
<i>I couldn't just leave it there.</i>

43:58.858 --> 44:01.365
<i>So when Tom and I got separated
in the gallery,</i>

44:01.432 --> 44:03.970
<i>I went back into the dining
room and got the knife.</i>

44:04.038 --> 44:05.573
<i>But at that moment,</i>

44:05.642 --> 44:07.477
<i>Priscilla regained
consciousness after fainting.</i>

44:07.546 --> 44:09.515
<i>She started
to become hysterical.</i>

44:09.583 --> 44:11.756
<i>I knew I couldn't
risk her revealing</i>

44:11.823 --> 44:14.060
<i>that I had engineered
this whole gathering...</i>

44:14.128 --> 44:15.397
<i>so I killed her.</i>

44:15.464 --> 44:16.900
<i>And I hid her in Tom's room.</i>

44:16.968 --> 44:18.571
<i>I tried to plant the knife</i>

44:18.638 --> 44:20.343
<i>in Tom's suitcase,
but at that moment,</i>

44:20.411 --> 44:22.548
<i>Muriel walked in,
caught me in the act.</i>

44:22.616 --> 44:24.419
<i>It wasn't her fault,
poor thing,</i>

44:24.486 --> 44:26.122
<i>but she had to die.</i>

44:26.190 --> 44:27.191
<i>I stabbed her,</i>

44:27.259 --> 44:28.829
<i>and she screamed.</i>

44:28.897 --> 44:30.233
<i>I had to leave the knife</i>

44:30.301 --> 44:31.870
<i>in her, because
I couldn't very well</i>

44:31.938 --> 44:34.009
<i>hide it on my person with
everyone quickly closing in.</i>

44:34.077 --> 44:37.381
<i>So I wiped off
the fingerprints and ran.</i>

44:37.450 --> 44:39.623
<i>I slipped in
with the rest of the group,</i>

44:39.690 --> 44:41.660
<i>when they all converged
on the scene.</i>

44:41.728 --> 44:44.734
<i>I needed more time
to finish my work framing Tom.</i>

44:44.801 --> 44:47.206
<i>But that's when Derek
went out to the balcony.</i>

44:47.273 --> 44:49.112
<i>I couldn't let him
contact the police</i>

44:49.179 --> 44:50.582
<i>before everything
was in the place.</i>

44:50.650 --> 44:52.920
<i>So I had to kill him, too.</i>

44:52.988 --> 44:54.622
<i>When Peter was yelling
at everyone</i>

44:54.690 --> 44:57.295
<i>about that picture of Derek
holding up the Hollywood sign,</i>

44:57.363 --> 45:00.404
<i>I grabbed the Golden Globe
and slipped out.</i>

45:00.471 --> 45:03.077
<i>I followed Derek outside
and did what I had to do.</i>

45:06.751 --> 45:08.857
<i>I barely had enough time
to plant the Golden Globe</i>

45:08.925 --> 45:10.227
<i>in Tom's room and run back
downstairs,</i>

45:10.295 --> 45:12.732
<i>where I took advantage
of the commotion</i>

45:12.800 --> 45:14.036
<i>and joined the crowd</i>

45:14.104 --> 45:16.607
<i>as they were all running
outside.</i>

45:16.675 --> 45:18.513
<i>And the rest...</i>

45:18.581 --> 45:21.253
<i>well, you did
all the rest for me.</i>

45:21.321 --> 45:24.526
<i>You turned on Tom
exactly as I planned.</i>

45:24.595 --> 45:26.064
So there it is, Lois.

45:26.132 --> 45:28.572
My God.

45:28.639 --> 45:31.512
But wait, there's one
thing unaccounted for--

45:31.580 --> 45:33.548
what happened to
Stephanie's body?

45:33.616 --> 45:35.652
Actually, that's
the one thing I don't know.

45:38.229 --> 45:39.430
Damn it!

45:41.168 --> 45:44.040
Well, now you know
everything, Lois.

45:44.108 --> 45:46.313
Which, of course, means
I have to kill you.

45:51.258 --> 45:52.425
Lois, are you coming?

45:52.493 --> 45:54.230
I can't play my tapes
without the key.

45:54.298 --> 45:56.571
Well, actually, Lois and I
were just about to go

45:56.639 --> 45:58.842
for a quick walk,
weren't we, Lois?

45:58.910 --> 46:00.446
We've been getting
better acquainted.

46:00.514 --> 46:02.116
All right, well, just
give me the key, please.

46:02.185 --> 46:04.420
All right, Peter,
I'll get it.

46:04.488 --> 46:06.761
Don't put a gun in my back.

46:06.829 --> 46:09.033
I'm not, I'm just
asking for the key.
Give me the key.

46:09.100 --> 46:11.037
<i>Peter, we've been
married 20 years.</i>

46:11.104 --> 46:13.075
<i>Please recognize when I'm
acting out of the ordinary</i>

46:13.143 --> 46:14.544
<i>because I'm in danger.</i>

46:14.612 --> 46:18.121
Here you go.
Here's the key, Pete.

46:18.189 --> 46:19.725
<i>Why is she calling me Pete?</i>

46:19.793 --> 46:21.529
<i>We been married 14 years.
She never called me Pete.</i>

46:21.597 --> 46:23.166
<i>Why am I trying to
figure this out</i>

46:23.234 --> 46:25.273
<i>when I could be listening
to my tapes in the car?</i>

46:25.341 --> 46:26.174
Bye.

46:27.612 --> 46:29.515
Shall we?

47:03.864 --> 47:07.036
Well, it's a shame that
you have to die, Lois,

47:07.104 --> 47:08.773
but look on the bright side:

47:08.841 --> 47:11.613
You'll be a story
on the 6:00 news.

47:11.681 --> 47:13.920
You know, unless a local
cat does something funny.

47:13.988 --> 47:16.426
Diane, please,
please, don't do this!

47:16.494 --> 47:18.897
I won't tell anybody,
I swear to God!

47:18.965 --> 47:21.838
That's right. You won't.

47:21.905 --> 47:23.343
Good-bye, Lois.

47:52.045 --> 47:53.647
Hello?

47:56.455 --> 47:58.491
Is anyone there?

48:03.605 --> 48:07.480
Whoever you are-- thank you!

48:15.500 --> 48:18.940
If anybody's gonna take that
